{
  "summary": "Encloses all non-comment header contents within `#ifndef`/`#endif` include guards and adjusts Doxygen file-level comment formatting across multiple headers. Updates `test/lint/lint-include-guards.py` to flag any non-empty, non-`//` lines located outside include guards.",
  "problem": "Several headers place includes, code, or namespace closures outside their include guards, preventing compilers from applying once-only header optimizations. Additionally, several headers had improper Doxygen `@file` formatting, and existing lint checks did not prevent content from slipping outside include guards.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description cites GCC documentation on once-only header optimization: 'From https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/cpp/Once-Only-Headers.html'",
    "PR description notes: 'A prerequisite for https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36808.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [
      "#36815"
    ],
    "enables": [
      "#36808"
    ]
  },
  "scope_notes": "Combines include guard structural fixes with Doxygen comment refactoring across 15 header files and an update to the python include-guard linter.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Added Doxygen file-level documentation cleanups across several header files (converting block comments to `//` lines and standardizing `@file` / `@brief` usage) to satisfy the stricter linter rules.",
  "card": "Encloses all header content within include guards and updates test/lint/lint-include-guards.py to enforce that no non-comment lines exist outside header guards. Also standardizes Doxygen file comment formatting across multiple headers so they pass the linter. This enables compiler once-only header optimization and prevents future guard regressions. The change is based on PR 36815 and is a prerequisite for PR 36808.",
